Modifications made by Haybarn
-----------------------------

Haybarn is maintained as a hard fork of duckdb/duckdb. All Haybarn-specific
changes are kept as a small, curated commit stack on top of an upstream DuckDB
release tag. As of the current release (built from DuckDB v1.5.3) those changes
are:

  * branding: rename artifacts to Haybarn
      The CLI is built as `haybarn`, the libraries as `libhaybarn` /
      `libhaybarn_static`, and the bundled static library as
      `libhaybarn_bundle.a`. The C++ `duckdb::` namespace, exported symbols,
      public header names, and the extension/database file formats are
      deliberately unchanged. Windows resource metadata is rebranded and the
      DuckDB logo icon is no longer referenced.

  * branding: Haybarn CLI banner and user-agent
      The interactive shell prints "Haybarn <version> — powered by DuckDB
      v<version>"; the default HTTP user-agent is "haybarn/...".

  * signing: replace embedded extension keys with the Haybarn key
      DuckDB's core and community extension-signing public keys are removed and
      replaced with a single Haybarn-controlled signing key. Only extensions
      signed by Haybarn will verify and load.

  * signing: repoint extension repositories to haybarn.query.farm
      The default and community extension repository URLs point at Haybarn's
      own repositories. The upstream "nightly" repository is removed.

  * ci: Haybarn release/extensions/python/publish workflows
      New GitHub Actions workflows that build, sign, and publish Haybarn
      artifacts.

  * ci: neuter upstream-only workflow triggers on the fork
      Auto-triggers are stripped from upstream DuckDB CI workflows that are not
      reused by Haybarn.

  * packaging: rename bundled static-library outputs

  * Python package rebranding (tools/pythonpkg): package and import name
      `haybarn`, compiled module renamed, opt-in `haybarn.compat` shim.

The authoritative, line-level record of every modification is the git history
of this fork (the commit stack on top of the upstream `v1.5.3` tag).


